markdown <<MARKDOWN
<h1>Troubleshooting Hardware</h1>

<p>In this lesson's main activity, your students troubleshoot a hardware problem for a client they met in Lesson 1. They work with a partner and use a four-step strategy called SNOT, which gives them a way to narrow down a problem instead of guessing. Students record their thinking in the <a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1B7ouAvwOxtIZBm0ljX2x4geEcscIk0xQwvzmmRL1D8g/edit?usp=sharing" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Troubleshooting Hardware Issues activity guide (Google Doc)</a>.</p><br>

<div style="background-color:#F7F7FB; border-left:4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius:8px; padding:12px 16px;">
<p>📖 <b>Troubleshooting</b> is a form of problem solving that uses a logical, systematic search for the source of a problem.</p>
</div>

<div style="background-color:#F7F7FB; border-left:4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius:8px; padding:12px 16px; margin-top:12px;">
<p>📖 <b>Decomposition</b> is breaking a larger problem into smaller, more manageable parts.</p>
</div>

<h2>The Four Steps</h2>

<p>Each step shrinks the list of possible causes. That is decomposition in action.</p>

<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(4, 1fr); gap:12px; margin:20px 0;">
<div style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:8px; align-items:flex-start; background-color:#F7F7FB; border-radius:10px; padding:12px 16px;">
<div style="flex-shrink:0; width:44px; height:44px; background-color:#4C42CF; color:#FFFFFF; border-radius:10px; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; font-size:20px; font-weight:700;">S</div>
<div style="font-size:16px;">
<p><b>Self</b></p>
<p>Restate the problem in your own words and make your best guesses about the cause.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:8px; align-items:flex-start; background-color:#F7F7FB; border-radius:10px; padding:12px 16px;">
<div style="flex-shrink:0; width:44px; height:44px; background-color:#4C42CF; color:#FFFFFF; border-radius:10px; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; font-size:20px; font-weight:700;">N</div>
<div style="font-size:16px;">
<p><b>Neighbor</b></p>
<p>Talk through the problem with a partner to compare ideas and rule out unlikely causes.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:8px; align-items:flex-start; background-color:#F7F7FB; border-radius:10px; padding:12px 16px;">
<div style="flex-shrink:0; width:44px; height:44px; background-color:#4C42CF; color:#FFFFFF; border-radius:10px; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; font-size:20px; font-weight:700;">O</div>
<div style="font-size:16px;">
<p><b>Online</b></p>
<p>Check a message board, a chat, and a user manual for evidence that supports or rules out a cause.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:8px; align-items:flex-start; background-color:#F7F7FB; border-radius:10px; padding:12px 16px;">
<div style="flex-shrink:0; width:44px; height:44px; background-color:#4C42CF; color:#FFFFFF; border-radius:10px; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; font-size:20px; font-weight:700;">T</div>
<div style="font-size:16px;">
<p><b>Technical Expert</b></p>
<p>Ask questions in an AI chat, the way an expert would, to gather information and eliminate more causes.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<h2>Meet the Clients</h2>

<p>Each student pair chooses one client from Lesson 1 and stays with that person through the whole activity. The clients have different hardware problems, but every one of them follows the same four steps.</p>

<div style="display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; justify-content:center; gap:12px; margin:20px 0;">
<div style="flex:1 1 170px; max-width:200px; background-color:#F7F7FB; border-radius:10px; padding:10px;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/98dd51673036f0dda8f22c3b0d840952-Amara.jpg" alt="A veterinarian checking a handheld device beside a truck at a farm" style="width:100%; height:auto; border-radius:10px;">
<div style="font-size:16px;">
<p><b>Amara Wanjiru</b></p>
<p>A veterinarian whose digital records go missing.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div style="flex:1 1 170px; max-width:200px; background-color:#F7F7FB; border-radius:10px; padding:10px;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/bc5dd713e9443613ea540a6e24dcd72c-Joaquin.jpg" alt="A coach holding a tablet while athletes run on a field behind him" style="width:100%; height:auto; border-radius:10px;">
<div style="font-size:16px;">
<p><b>Joaquín Silva</b></p>
<p>A coach whose player tracking hardware has problems.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div style="flex:1 1 170px; max-width:200px; background-color:#F7F7FB; border-radius:10px; padding:10px;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/73c28b3e33331edfaaeee5b1c37ccc3f-Denise.jpg" alt="A farmer holding a tablet in a field with a drone flying overhead" style="width:100%; height:auto; border-radius:10px;">
<div style="font-size:16px;">
<p><b>Denise Carter</b></p>
<p>A farmer whose drone is taking faulty images.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div style="flex:1 1 170px; max-width:200px; background-color:#F7F7FB; border-radius:10px; padding:10px;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/7676b550d756dd303d7799208583c0e3-Marcus.jpg" alt="A visualization supervisor drawing on a tablet in front of several monitors" style="width:100%; height:auto; border-radius:10px;">
<div style="font-size:16px;">
<p><b>Marcus Reyes</b></p>
<p>A visualization supervisor whose special effects will not render properly.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div style="flex:1 1 170px; max-width:200px; background-color:#F7F7FB; border-radius:10px; padding:10px;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/acc07e0dc87ecaeb26fd4ed5958febc4-Layla.jpg" alt="A pharmacist scanning a medicine package at a pharmacy counter" style="width:100%; height:auto; border-radius:10px;">
<div style="font-size:16px;">
<p><b>Layla Haddad</b></p>
<p>A pharmacist whose pill dispensing machine is having problems.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div style="background-color:#E4E2F8; border-radius:10px; padding:12px 16px; margin:20px 0;">
<div style="font-size:16px; color:#222222;">
<p><b>💡 Teacher tip:</b> If students jump to a first guess, point them back to the Guess Who? warm-up. The strongest questions eliminate the most possibilities at once, and every SNOT step should shorten the list of possible causes.</p>
</div>
</div>

<p><i>Next, follow one client through all four steps to see exactly what your students will do.</i></p>
MARKDOWN
